      <h3 id="case-poc-setting-title">Evaluation setting</h3>
      <div class="report-prose">
        <p>
          We further evaluate a composite task that requires placing a bookmark and a pen on the
          same open book. <strong>Bookmark on Book</strong> and pen-placement tasks with other
          targets (a pen holder or a ruler) appear in the robot-policy training set, whereas{' '}
          <strong>Pen on Book</strong> does not. This setting therefore tests more than the
          sequencing of two familiar tasks: the combined objective includes an atomic task absent
          from the robot-policy training data.
        </p>
        <p>
          The prescribed sequence places the bookmark first and then the pen. We evaluate each
          method over <strong>10 rollouts</strong> using zero-shot execution of the composite task;
          GPT-6-Astra receives no in-context demonstrations. Partial credit of 0.5 points is awarded
          for correctly completing the first object placement in the prescribed sequence.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
